  "$comment": "Dig & Discover tuning (GDD §17: everything configurable). Distances in world units (1 block = 1 unit). materials: durability = hit points, minPower = weakest tool power that can dig it, value = sell price per item, drops = items per block; block = the KayKit block model drawn for it, pickup = what flies into the backpack, decor = pieces poking out of the top (nuggets on ores, gems on crystals) so they read from above. zones: rings around the hub by distance (from = where the zone starts; edges are wobbly); fill = the zone's base rock (its minPower gates the zone behind a tool tier), patches/ores = {id, chance} mixed in, findChance = share of blocks hiding a find. finds: the artifacts to collect (GDD §11) — 3 per zone (`zone`, 0-based), buried and revealed when a tunnel reaches them, worth `reward` cash; `weight` = relative odds within the zone, `rarity` drives the find banner. The collection totem in the hub shows found vs missing; finding them all completes the collection (`collectionReward`). wardrobe: looks bought with cash at the hub closet (colors, faces under images/non-preload/skins, hats under models/hats; hat placement in ui/hatfits.json).",
